#
# A path allowlist ("ignore *.spec.ts") would hide a real credential pasted into
# a spec file tomorrow, which is the failure mode this gate exists to catch. A
# fingerprint is `<file>:<rule>:<line>`, so it excuses exactly the occurrence
# below and nothing else: move the line, add a second secret to the same file,
# or introduce a new rule hit, and the gate fires again.
#
# Every entry was read before being written here. All fifteen are canonical
# documentation placeholders — `AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE`, `ghp_0123456789…`,
# `AIzaSyD-1234…` — and most of them are fixtures for the redaction tests
# themselves, i.e. the input a test feeds to the code that scrubs secrets.
#
# Re-derive after a legitimate change with:
#   gitleaks dir . --no-banner --redact --report-format json --report-path /tmp/gl.json

